<title>GERMANY: W.German Nov industry output up 2.0 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>W.German Nov industry output up 2.0 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> W.GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT    Nov 96     Oct 96     Nov 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)   +2.0	 -0.6	 +0.7</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +2.1	 +0.9	  n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		96.5	 94.6	 94.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank statistics. @ The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				     Nov 96		  Oct 96</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Mining		     86.8	 +3.0     84.3	 +1.4</p>
<p> Manufacturing output   96.1	 +2.5     93.8	 -1.0</p>
<p> Incl:Intermed. goods  101.0	 +2.5     98.5	 -0.1</p>
<p>	Capital goods     95.6	 +2.8     93.0	 -2.1</p>
<p>	Consumer durables 84.9	 +4.4     81.3	 -1.5</p>
<p>	Consumer goods    90.9	 +0.8     90.2	 -1.1</p>
<p> Energy output	   108.3	 +0.5    107.8	 +3.1</p>
<p> Construction	     93.8	 -2.3     96.0	 -0.3 @</p>
<p>Two month comparison Oct/Nov 96 with Aug/Sept 96:</p>
<p>    Industrial production	    unch @</p>
<p>Two month comparison Oct/Nov 96 with Oct/Nov 95:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     +1.3</p>
<p> Mining				    -2.5</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		 +2.1</p>
<p>  Including:Intermediate goods     +2.9</p>
<p>		Capital goods	    +2.6</p>
<p>		Consumer durables	+3.7</p>
<p>		Consumer goods	   -1.2</p>
<p> Energy output			   +5.3</p>
<p> Construction			    -8.6</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
